{
  "quest.10E9ABD23A1018AC.title": "&cBuilding a Reactor",
  "quest.6743DD04E257193E.title": "&cPorts",
  "quest.4E45AACCDF8A2570.title": "&aColossal Reactors",
  "quest.79AF583F5A5822F5.title": "&aReactor Alloys",
  "quest.724B135686CA1EC9.quest_desc": [
    "Every &aUranium Ingot&r the reactor burns becomes one &2Nuclear Waste&r, and the waste stays inside the reactor until something takes it out. If it backs up, the reactor stops making power.",
    "",
    "Set a &aResource Port&r to Extract with the Waste filter and put a hopper or pipe on its outside face, or empty the waste by hand from the &2Reactor Controller&r. After changing a port's mode or filter, press Reboot on the controller so it picks up the change.",
    "",
    "Waste is not a dead end. Craft it into &aAzurite Ingots&r and put those back in the rods as fuel. Azurite has a base rate of 1,000 RF/t against Uranium's 400, but each ingot holds only a third as much fuel.",
  ],
  "quest.74935522E3445523.title": "&bTurbines",
  "quest.74935522E3445523.quest_desc": [
    "A turbine is the second multiblock. It takes the steam from a water-cooled reactor and turns it into more power than the reactor would have made on its own.",
    "",
    "Inside the casing goes a shaft of &aTurbine Rods&r, with exactly one &2Turbine Rod Controller&r at the center of the top rotor layer. The turbine will not form without it.",
    "",
    "Right-click a rod with &aTurbine Blades&r to add them. Each blade lets the turbine take up to 48 mB of steam a tick, but blades only count in complete rings of four around a rod, so a half-finished ring adds nothing.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The top layers inside are the coil zone. Fill them with metal storage blocks, and better metals give more power per mB of steam. Empty space there only counts for 30%, and &aHeating Coils&r count the same as empty space.",
    "",
    "It has its own Power, Resource and Redstone ports, plus a &aHigh Conduction Power Port&r for large builds.",
  ],
  "quest.779D59424131B19B.quest_desc": [
    "The &aReactor Builder&r and &2Turbine Builder&r will assemble a valid structure for you if you would rather not work out the geometry for these yourself.",
  ],
  "quest.4D1112009773016A.title": "&bCoolant and Steam",
  "quest.79AF583F5A5822F5.quest_desc": [
    "Raw metal won't hold a reactor together. The casing, rods and controllers are all made from alloys, so the metals you gathered need refining first.",
    "",
    "Alloy your first batch of both. &aTough Alloy&r goes into the reactor's casing, rods and controller, and &2Stainless Steel&r into the turbine's casing and blades.",
    "",
    "The &aMelter&r turns &2Breeze Rods&r into &bRefrigerant Gelid Breezium&r, the heat sink that gives reactor rods the biggest power boost. It needs a heat source on at least one side, and lava or a campfire works until you have Heating Coils.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The Unrefined alloy crafting and blasting recipes are turned off in this pack, so both ingots come from an alloy machine such as the &eEnder IO&r Alloy Smelter or the &eEnergized Power&r Alloy Furnace.",
  ],
  "quest.779D59424131B19B.title": "Auto-builders",
  "quest.6743DD04E257193E.quest_desc": [
    "A reactor talks to the outside world through ports set into its casing.",
    "",
    "- &aPower Port&r pushes energy out, and the &2High Conduction&r version pushes far more of it.",
    "- &aResource Port&r takes fuel in and waste out.",
    "- &aRedstone Port&r lets you control the thing from a signal.",
    "",
    "One of each is the minimum for a reactor that runs without you standing next to it.",
  ],
  "quest.724B135686CA1EC9.title": "&2Nuclear Waste",
  "quest.4D1112009773016A.quest_desc": [
    "To run a turbine, the reactor has to make steam instead of power. Pipe &bWater&r into a &aResource Port&r set to Insert with the Coolant filter, and pull &bSteam&r out of a second port set to Extract with the Coolant filter.",
    "",
    "The steam comes out of the reactor's own power output. The more water it turns into steam, the less RF its Power Port sends, and it can drop to nothing while the fuel still burns.",
    "",
    "&bRefrigerant Gelid Breezium&r is not a coolant. It is a heat sink. Fill empty cells inside the reactor with source blocks of it and the rods next to them make more power than with any other heat sink. Flowing breezium does not count.",
    "",
    "&aHeating Coils&r are not reactor parts. They heat the &aMelter&r from any side. The Energy coil runs on power and the Resource coil uses up items or fluids, and both heat it faster than lava.",
  ],
  "quest.4E45AACCDF8A2570.quest_desc": [
    "&eColossal Reactors&r builds power out of two multiblocks you design yourself. A &creactor&r burns fuel, and a &bturbine&r turns its steam into a great deal more energy than the reactor makes alone.",
    "",
    "Neither has a fixed shape. You decide what goes inside, and the output follows from those choices.",
    "",
    "Start by gathering the metals. &aUranium&r, &2Lead&r, Boron, Chromium and Graphite all go into the build.",
  ],
  "quest.10E9ABD23A1018AC.quest_desc": [
    "A reactor is a hollow box of &aReactor Casing&r with a &2Reactor Controller&r in the wall and Reactor Rods running top to bottom inside it. It can be at most &e32x32x32&r, casing included.",
    "",
    "&aReactor Glass&r lets you see in. Each column of rods needs a &aReactor Rod Controller&r in the top layer of casing, directly above it, and every block under it in that column must be a rod or the reactor will not form.",
    "",
    "Feed it &aUranium&r and it makes power, plus &2Nuclear Waste&r you will need to deal with.",
  ],
}